[1960.113355, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[5Gcontent changes. There's no schedule\u001b[43Gext\u001b[47Gnsion\u001b[53Ginstalled,\u001b[64Gso\u001b[67Ga\u001b[69Glive\u001b[74Gsite\u001b[79Gwould\u001b[85Gneed\u001b[90Ga\u001b[92Gcron\u001b[97Gjob.\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mThe search page \u001b[23Gading still reads \"Search\".\u001b[22m The design has \"Search results for “…”\" as the he\u001b[101Gding;\r\u001b[4C\u001b[1Bf\u001b[7Gr now\u001b[13Gt\u001b[16Gt wording appears in the line above the results.\u001b[K\r\u001b[14C\u001b[1B\u001b[1m-box plugin's\u001b[29G\"F\u001b[33Gte\u001b[36Gs\" field still refers to the filter by record ID.\u001b[86G\u001b[22mIt's\u001b[91Gcorrect after a\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bresh impor\u001b[17G, where it's the\u001b[34Go\u001b[36Gly fi\u001b[42Gter, and the README \u001b[63Gays\u001b[67Gso.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[1mTwo bugs from earlier stages, not fixed:\u001b[22m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B1.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mThe page IDs in the site settings are wrong on a fresh install.\u001b[70G\u001b[22mThe\u001b[74GREADME\u001b[81Gsays\u001b[86Ga\u001b[88Gfresh\u001b[94Gimport\u001b[101Gkeeps\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B   the same IDs, but it doesn't. Search landed\u001b[50Gon\u001b[53G20\u001b[56Ginstead\u001b[64Gof\u001b[67G16,\u001b[71Gso\u001b[74Gthe\u001b[78Gheader\u001b[85Gsearch\u001b[92Gform\u001b[97Gsent\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B  \u001b[6Gpeople to \"Access to information\". The service and footer menus\u001b[70G(22/23) and the\u001b[86G404 page (33) ar\u001b[103G\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Balso off.\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B2.\u001b[6G\u001b[1mEvery news item gets the \"Education\" category on a fresh install,\u001b[22m on top of\u001b[82Gits\u001b[86Greal on\u001b[94G.\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BShould I fix those two next? Otherwise I can commit this as \"Stage 09-search\" now.\u001b[86G\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m✻\u001b[3GChurned for 9m 33s · done 12:48 PM\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m※\u001b[3G\u001b[1mrecap: \u001b[22m\u001b[3mSite search now works with the free ke_search, tested on a fresh install, and is ready to commit \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bas \"Stage 09-search\". Your call: should I commit it now, or first fix two earlier-stage bugs that break \r\u001b[1B\u001b[23m\u001b[39m \u001b[3G\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m\u001b[3mthe header search o\u001b[23G fresh installs? (turn\u001b[46Goff recaps\u001b[57Gin /config)\u001b[23m\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m❯ \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mWhy does \"new\" not find anything?\u001b[39m                                                                       \r\u001b[2B\u001b[49m\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m●\u001b[39m Running \u001b[1m1\u001b[22m shell command…\u001b[K\r\u001b[12C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m3\u001b[39m\u001b[31;1H\u001b[29;3H\u001b[?25h"]
